{"case_id":"C016","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["input semantics","API validation","undefined behavior in harness"],"confidence":97,"affected_functions":["spng_decoded_image_size","LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput"],"reason":"H0 does not reliably fuzz the full invalid `fmt` integer domain implicated by S1. It constructs `fmt` only as `1 << (data[size - 2] & 31)`, so it excludes multi-bit and most negative values handled by the `fmt & ((unsigned)fmt - 1)` validation. The shift is also performed on signed `int`; when the shift count is 31, the harness itself can invoke undefined behavior instead of reliably supplying the `INT_MIN`-like case for which the unsigned arithmetic matters.","evidence":["S1 changes `fmt & (fmt - 1)` to `fmt & ((unsigned)fmt - 1)` inside `spng_decoded_image_size()`, directly implicating signed-range and invalid-format semantics.","H0 derives `fmt` with `int fmt = data[size - 2] & 31; fmt = 1 << fmt;`, restricting inputs to nominal single-bit patterns.","The validation comment and `if(fmt & ((unsigned)fmt - 1)) return SPNG_EFMT` explicitly concern values having more than one bit set, but H0 never intentionally generates such values.","For a shift count of 31, `1 << fmt` uses signed `int` arithmetic and is not a reliable way to construct the relevant high-bit value."],"recommended_action":"Fuzz `spng_decoded_image_size()` with a raw, safely constructed full-range `int` format value, including zero, valid constants, multi-bit combinations, arbitrary negative values, `INT_MIN`, and `INT_MAX`; avoid signed left-shift by decoding bytes into an unsigned value and converting explicitly."}
